---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="Eligibility, scoring, disclosure classification, and correction methods for Slop Factor."
>
  <article class="shell prose-page">
    <header class="prose-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
      <h1>Methodology</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Public records are based on explicit author disclosures and reproducible
        structural counts. Candidate matching is only a review aid.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="on-this-page" aria-label="On this page">
      <strong>On this page</strong>
      <a href="#eligibility">Eligibility</a>
      <a href="#score">Score</a>
      <a href="#classification">Disclosure classification</a>
      <a href="#counting">Counting methods</a>
      <a href="#corrections">Corrections</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="eligibility">
      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        A paper is eligible for the public dataset only when every condition
        below is met:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Its primary arXiv category begins with <code>math.</code>.</li>
        <li>
          The paper or official arXiv metadata explicitly discloses author use
          of AI or an LLM.
        </li>
        <li>
          A human reviewer verifies that the passage is an author disclosure
          rather than a citation or general discussion.
        </li>
        <li>
          The exact disclosure quotation and its page or metadata location are
          recorded.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Search matches remain private review candidates. No detector,
        probability estimate, or inferred use can make a paper eligible.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="score">
      <h2>Slop Factor</h2>
      <div
        class="formula"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Slop Factor equals M times the sum of P, six T, four L, four Q, three C, two D, E over four, R over ten, and two A."
      >
        <span
          >Slop Factor = M × (P + 6T + 4L + 4Q + 3C + 2D + E/4 + R/10 + 2A)</span
        >
      </div>
      <dl class="definition-list">
        <div><dt>P</dt><dd>Total PDF pages</dd></div>
        <div><dt>T</dt><dd>Theorems</dd></div>
        <div><dt>L</dt><dd>Lemmas</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Q</dt><dd>Propositions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>C</dt><dd>Corollaries</dd></div>
        <div><dt>D</dt><dd>Definitions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>E</dt><dd>Displayed equations</dd></div>
        <div><dt>R</dt><dd>Bibliography entries</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A</dt><dd>Appendix pages</dd></div>
        <div><dt>M</dt><dd>Disclosure multiplier</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>
        The score is unbounded. It is not normalized and is not an AI
        probability, an originality measure, or a judgment of correctness or
        quality.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="classification">
      <h2>Disclosure classification</h2>
      <div class="method-table">
        <table>
          <thead
            ><tr
              ><th scope="col">Multiplier</th><th scope="col">Disclosed role</th
              ></tr
            ></thead
          >
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>Proofreading, grammar, or translation</td></tr>
            <tr
              ><td>2</td><td>Brainstorming, literature assistance, or code</td
              ></tr
            >
            <tr><td>5</td><td>Rewriting or drafting portions</td></tr>
            <tr
              ><td>10</td><td
                >Substantial text, proofs, or content generation</td
              ></tr
            >
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        When several disclosed uses apply, the highest applicable multiplier is
        used. A reviewer may select an intermediate multiplier when the
        disclosure falls materially between the listed categories; the record
        must state the rationale.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="counting">
      <h2>Counting methods</h2>
      <p>
        The analysis prefers arXiv source files. It counts theorem-like and
        displayed-equation LaTeX environments, bibliography entries, and page
        structure after safely extracting the source archive. PDF pages and
        appendix boundaries are obtained from the rendered PDF.
      </p>
      <p>
        When source is unavailable or cannot be parsed, PDF-text patterns
        provide fallback estimates. Each record identifies the method used for
        every count and documents material limitations. Validation recalculates
        every score from the stored counts and multiplier.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="corrections">
      <h2>Correction policy</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections are accepted for disclosure transcription, classification,
        document counts, metadata, and version changes. A correction should
        identify the arXiv record and provide the relevant page, source passage,
        or reproducible count. Approved records are updated through reviewable
        version-control changes, with the previous history retained.
      </p>
      <p>
        Inclusion is not criticism of a paper or its authors. It records an
        explicit disclosure and applies a documented structural formula; it does
        not evaluate mathematical merit.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
